{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Of Asher, rich is his bread.</b> His food is rich (fat) on account of the abundance of olives that is in the portion of Asher, and it draws oil like a spring. And so Moses our teacher of blessed memory interpreted (Deuteronomy 33:24): ״וטובל בשמן רגלו״ — and it would have been fitting for the verse to say 'אשר שמנה לחמו.'" "<b>Rather,</b> it is possible to say a reason for the addition of the מם (in מאשר), that it comes to indicate the extraordinary degree of the matter — for it is not necessary to say that the blessing of the abundance of oil should be in the portion of Asher alone, but rather that even in the other lands the blessing of the abundance of oil from the portion of Asher will be found. And this is the reason for the addition of the מם, for from it flows the abundance of oil, and from it it is conveyed to the other lands."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:21:37.466873263Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}